725 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 438 0 R
/E (How is SOS/EOS mathematically defined? We used the Amplitude-Fraction Method. We find the lowest "baseline" greenness and the "peak" greenness. The difference is the Seasonal Amplitude. SOS is the day when NDVI crosses a specific percentage of this amplitude on the way up. EOS is when it crosses on the way down.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
