/E (Raw remote sensing data \(MODIS, CHIRPS\) was extracted directly to capture essential climatic and phenological variables over Similipal. Temporal and spatial metrics \(ET, LST, Rainfall, NDVI, Phenometrics\) were converted into georeferenced raster image formats and imported into QGIS for multi-layered spatial visualisation, mapping out physical zones and variable intensities. This provides direct visual proof of how factors like moisture stress, surface temperatures, and rainfall correlate with the physical landscape of our Wet and Dry zones.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [1]
>>
